#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""CAD-959: enqueue a PR only when the AGENTS.md review and merge rules hold.

    scripts/enqueue-reviewed <pr> --head <full-40-hex-sha> [--repo owner/name]
                             [--notes-dir DIR] [--author ALIAS ...]
                             [--dry-run] [--poll-secs N] [--poll-interval N]

Every `cadence` call uses the build named by CADENCE_BIN (default: `cadence` on
PATH), so a host that also carries a newer build can point the gate at it
instead of seeing hosted verbs reported as unavailable.

Refuses (exit 1, one reason per line on stderr, every failing rule listed)
unless ALL of these hold for the pinned head:

  * the PR is OPEN, its head equals --head, mergeStateStatus is not DIRTY and
    auto-merge is off;
  * every required status check of the base branch (branch protection AND
    rulesets) is PRESENT and SUCCESS at that head. Missing or pending fails,
    and so does a base branch for which no required check can be read: an
    invalid workflow yields zero checks, and "nothing failed" is not a pass;
  * the verdict notes in the notes dir, parsed by `cadence audit verdicts`
    (the audit's own note parser; reviewer = first token of `From:`), give the
    required count of PASS verdicts pinned to this exact head from distinct
    reviewers, none of them the PR author: two (Standards plus Spec/security),
    or one (`Review (standards+spec)`) when every change is on the one-review
    list (docs/roles/one-review-paths.toml, CAD-957, read with the diff's anchor:
    main's live tip for a PR based on main, else the PR's base commit, so a PR
    cannot widen its own list). A `ui/` change also needs a
    Browser QA pass. AOS-473: a document whose `origin` is `hosted` is counted
    by the owner's attestation instead — the row must name this repo and carry
    a reviewer_id and a github_login (except a CAD-2081 workflow-issued row,
    which carries no login and counts under its own rules; see AGENTS.md
    "Review"), distinct reviewers are principals, the
    author check compares the attested login, and one login fills at most one
    slot (two counted principals behind one login refuse the set). Two hosted
    rows of one reviewer and kind that share a stamp are refused unless they
    carry the same evidence, login included. A local document (or one from an
    older client, which has no marker) counts exactly as before. CAD-2001: the
    hosted reads are project-scoped. `cadence delivery requirements` says
    where its answer came from (`origin: "hosted"`), and the gate then passes
    the ticket's project — the one the requirements binding already names and
    this script already checks against the ticket — to `cadence audit
    verdicts --project` and `cadence audit approval --project --issue`. The
    project is never derived from the repo or the cwd, and a hosted read that
    cannot name it is refused rather than answered from repo-scoped evidence;
  * this gate is main's (CAD-2108): its own bytes and the sibling delivery-gate
    equal origin/main:scripts/<name>, read by local git from the current
    directory with no network. Differing, or a file unreadable on either side
    while origin/main exists, refuses (--dry-run warns and runs). No origin/main
    in the current directory means no check. A stale local origin/main is not
    detected. The first stdout line names the gate's content hash;
  * a ticket comment for this head lists those verdict notes (created after
    the other gates pass; dry-run only checks an existing comment);
  * for a human-class diff (a path trigger, more than 1500 changed lines, any
    head-pinned note whose Risk is not exactly `auto`, or a workflow-issued
    review on any change outside docs/roles/workflow-auto-paths.toml),
    `cadence audit approval` reports an approval in
    force for exactly this head. This script never records an approval.

Review standard (operator decision 2026-11-03, CAD-1946): a valid review is a
fresh-context session that is not the author, a subagent included (AGENTS.md
"Review"). This gate does not enforce that: hosted verdicts count by attested
principal and the author's is refused, local notes count by their self-declared
`From:` alias (not attested), so it cannot tell a fresh session from the author
under one login. CAD-2081 adds workflow-issued rows (see AGENTS.md "Review"); their
workflows (CAD-2088) are live, a cheap first pass beside fresh-session reviews on
gate, security, schema and release PRs, and two of them satisfy other PRs. On
hosted today `routine` and `ui/**` PRs still need the temporary exception below,
which runs to 2026-12-31.

CAD-1946 temporary exception: `--exception --advisory standards=<url> --advisory
spec-security=<url>` (and `browser-qa=<url>` for a `ui/` change) waives only the
missing authenticated reviewer attestation, and on a hosted routine PR the readiness
proof hosted can't produce yet, which the evidence names. Every other rule still
holds, a filed non-pass verdict still refuses, the operator must have approved this exact head
(no scope fallback), and the signature and evidence say it is an exception. The
advisory links are findings from separately assigned sessions, not verdicts: the
gate cannot prove they are fresh sessions, and the operator accepts that. The
exception only checks that the links are separate https URLs: it proves neither
head binding nor that Browser QA ran. Ends at
`EXCEPTION_ENDS` in scripts/delivery-gate.

CAD-2001 release order: the tenant server must serve the project-scoped gate
verbs before this client sends them. An older tenant refuses the verb names
(HTTP 501/400/409/503) and the client says so — "update the tenant server
first, then this Cadence client" — which this gate reports as a refusal, never
as "no evidence was filed" and never by falling back to the repo-scoped reads.

Then it signs (repo, pr, head) with the delivery-gate key (--gate-key) and posts
the signature on the PR (CAD-1925: the merge queue's `delivery-gate` job holds
any PR without it), runs `gh pr merge --auto --squash --match-head-commit <sha>`, polls
isInMergeQueue for up to --poll-secs (default 30), and when the PR is not
queued runs --disable-auto and exits 1. --dry-run runs every check and
enqueues nothing. Exit: 0 enqueued (or dry-run clean) / 1 refused / 2 usage.
"""

